window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b240-c3a1f5971070abfe.json"]={sha256:"c3a1f5971070abfe1e441441d0b0884645b0ee8083d78a24d09189d55b314c5f",value:{"id":"b240","title":"大壩施工導流","titleEn":"River diversion during dam construction","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以大壩施工導流為入口，深入施工導流的洪水暴露、過流能力與階段轉換。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。","summaryEn":"Using River diversion during dam construction as its entry point, this course examines diversion flood exposure, hydraulic capacity and construction transitions. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-systems","subcategoryTitle":"防潮、航運與大壩施工","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-systems","learningTags":["water","water-systems","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["施工期洪水暴露","Construction-period flood exposure"],["滿流隧洞的沿程損失","Full-flow tunnel friction loss"],["圍堰底部的揚壓作用","Cofferdam base uplift"],["截流缺口的流速放大","Closure-gap velocity amplification"],["導流切換與關鍵工期","Diversion transitions and critical duration"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["施工期洪水暴露","滿流隧洞的沿程損失","圍堰底部的揚壓作用","截流缺口的流速放大","導流切換與關鍵工期"],"labelsEn":["Construction-period flood exposure","Full-flow tunnel friction loss","Cofferdam base uplift","Closure-gap velocity amplification","Diversion transitions and critical duration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"本課原創比較練習分兩個相互獨立的物理模型。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每年超越機率0.05、各年獨立且平穩，三年內至少一次超越1−(1−0.05)³=0.142625即14.2625%；不代表季節施工窗口機率。教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：SI制曼寧係數n的單位為s/m^(1/3)。假設矩形渠寬10 m、水深3 m、曼寧n=0.025、坡度0.001，A=30 m²、R=30/16=1.875 m，Q=AR^(2/3)S^0.5/n=57.701 m³/s；均勻流。先逐一圈出公式內的控制體、力方向或時間尺度，再把每項輸入的量綱換成一致單位。第二人只根據輸入重算結果，不抄第一人的中間數字。最後指出這兩個估算尚未包含的空間變化、非線性及量測誤差；若將結果用於另一座工程，必須重建其幾何、材料與邊界條件，不能挪用本練習的假設。 導流渠糙率敏感度固定寬10 m、水深3 m、坡度0.001，因此A=30 m²與R=1.875 m不變，只將曼寧n由0.025增至0.030 s/m^(1/3)。Q=AR^(2/3)S^0.5/n由57.701降至48.084 m³/s，約減少16.67%。這是指定水深下均勻流輸水能力的比較；若指定流量不變，應另解新水深，不能同時固定流量與水深。","textEn":"This original comparison exercise uses two independent physical models. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual exceedance probability 0.05 with independent stationary years. At least one exceedance in three years has probability 0.142625, or 14.2625 percent, not a seasonal-window probability. Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The SI Manning coefficient n has units s/m^(1/3). Assume rectangular width 10 m, depth 3 m, Manning n=0.025 and slope 0.001. Area is 30 m² and radius 1.875 m, giving uniform-flow capacity approximately 57.701 m³/s. First identify the control volume, force direction or time scale in each relation, then convert every input to consistent units. A second reviewer recalculates from the inputs without copying intermediate numbers. Finally identify spatial variability, nonlinear effects and measurement errors omitted by both estimates. Transfer to another structure requires rebuilding its geometry, material description and boundary conditions; the assumed classroom inputs are not transferable design or operating parameters. Hold channel width 10 m, depth 3 m and slope 0.001 fixed, retaining A=30 m² and R=1.875 m, and increase only Manning n from 0.025 to 0.030 s/m^(1/3). Uniform-flow capacity Q=AR^(2/3)S^0.5/n falls from 57.701 to 48.084 m³/s, approximately 16.67%. This compares capacity at prescribed depth; prescribing unchanged discharge instead requires solving for a new depth.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b240-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「施工期洪水暴露」與「明渠導流的過水能力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Construction-period flood exposure\" and \"Open-channel diversion capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b240-v15-01","title":"施工期洪水暴露：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Construction-period flood exposure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「施工期洪水暴露」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Construction-period flood exposure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"施工導流的風險與暴露時間及洪水季節分布有關，重現期不是保證多久才發生一次。短期工程仍可能遇到大洪水，且後果隨開挖、圍堰和永久壩體所處階段改變。 假設每年超越機率0.05、各年獨立且平穩，三年內至少一次超越1−(1−0.05)³=0.142625即14.2625%；不代表季節施工窗口機率。 把全年機率直接按月份等比例縮小會忽略季節集中，連續年份的氣候相關性也會破壞獨立假設。即使超越機率相同，不同階段的損失與恢復時間仍可能完全不同。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「施工期洪水暴露」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Diversion risk depends on exposure duration and seasonal flood distribution. Return period is not a guaranteed waiting time, and consequences change as excavation, cofferdams and permanent works pass through different construction stages. Assume annual exceedance probability 0.05 with independent stationary years. At least one exceedance in three years has probability 0.142625, or 14.2625 percent, not a seasonal-window probability. Dividing annual probability in proportion to months ignores seasonality, and climate persistence violates independence. Equal exceedance probabilities can also correspond to very different losses and recovery times at different stages of construction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Construction-period flood exposure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每年超越機率0.05、各年獨立且平穩，三年內至少一次超越1−(1−0.05)³=0.142625即14.2625%；不代表季節施工窗口機率。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual exceedance probability 0.05 with independent stationary years.","failure":"常見誤解：「二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「施工期洪水暴露」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Construction-period flood exposure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-01-k1","title":"施工期洪水暴露","titleEn":"Construction-period flood exposure","text":"施工導流的風險與暴露時間及洪水季節分布有關，重現期不是保證多久才發生一次。短期工程仍可能遇到大洪水，且後果隨開挖、圍堰和永久壩體所處階段改變。","textEn":"Diversion risk depends on exposure duration and seasonal flood distribution. Return period is not a guaranteed waiting time, and consequences change as excavation, cofferdams and permanent works pass through different construction stages.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「施工期洪水暴露」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Construction-period flood exposure\" is correct?","options":["二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。","施工導流的風險與暴露時間及洪水季節分布有關，重現期不是保證多久才發生一次。","導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。"],"optionsEn":["A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years.","Diversion risk depends on exposure duration and seasonal flood distribution.","Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"施工導流的風險與暴露時間及洪水季節分布有關，重現期不是保證多久才發生一次。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Diversion risk depends on exposure duration and seasonal flood distribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b240-v15-02","title":"施工期洪水暴露：定量估算","titleEn":"Construction-period flood exposure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「施工期洪水暴露」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Construction-period flood exposure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每年超越機率0.05、各年獨立且平穩，三年內至少一次超越1−(1−0.05)³=0.142625即14.2625%；不代表季節施工窗口機率。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual exceedance probability 0.05 with independent stationary years. At least one exceedance in three years has probability 0.142625, or 14.2625 percent, not a seasonal-window probability. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以施工階段對應水文資料期間，區分全年年最大值與特定月份事件；查核長期趨勢和上游調控變更，將每階段暴露、洪峰不確定度及淹水後果列成可追溯的風險表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Match construction stages to hydrologic records, distinguishing annual maxima from events in selected months.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每年超越機率0.05、各年獨立且平穩，三年內至少一次超越1−(1−0.05)³=0.142625即14.2625%；不代表季節施工窗口機率。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual exceedance probability 0.05 with independent stationary years. At least one exceedance in three years has probability 0.142625, or 14.2625 percent, not a seasonal-window probability.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「施工期洪水暴露」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Construction-period flood exposure\", which statement holds?","options":["入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。","兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每年超越機率0.05、各年獨立且平穩，三年內至少一次超越1−(1−0.05)³=0.142625即14.2625%。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent.","Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual exceedance probability 0.05 with independent stationary years."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每年超越機率0.05、各年獨立且平穩，三年內至少一次超越1−(1−0.05)³=0.142625即14.2625%；不代表季節施工窗口機率。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual exceedance probability 0.05 with independent stationary years. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b240-v15-03","title":"施工期洪水暴露：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Construction-period flood exposure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「施工期洪水暴露」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Construction-period flood exposure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以施工階段對應水文資料期間，區分全年年最大值與特定月份事件；查核長期趨勢和上游調控變更，將每階段暴露、洪峰不確定度及淹水後果列成可追溯的風險表。另列洪水樣本的季節涵蓋。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Match construction stages to hydrologic records, distinguishing annual maxima from events in selected months. Check long-term trends and upstream regulation changes, recording stage exposure, peak uncertainty and inundation consequences in a traceable risk assessment. Document seasonal coverage of the flood sample separately. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以施工期洪水暴露編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以施工階段對應水文資料期間，區分全年年最大值與特定月份事件；查核長期趨勢和上游調控變更，將每階段暴露、洪峰不確定度及淹水後果列成可追溯的風險表。另列洪水樣本的季節涵蓋。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for construction-period flood exposure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Match construction stages to hydrologic records, distinguishing annual maxima from events in selected months. Check long-term trends and upstream regulation changes, recording stage exposure, peak uncertainty and inundation consequences in a traceable risk assessment. Document seasonal coverage of the flood sample separately.","failure":"注意干擾：把全年機率直接按月份等比例縮小會忽略季節集中，連續年份的氣候相關性也會破壞獨立假設。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Dividing annual probability in proportion to months ignores seasonality, and climate persistence violates independence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以施工階段對應水文資料期間，區分全年年最大值與特定月份事件；查核長期趨勢和上游調控變更，將每階段暴露、洪峰不確定度及淹水後果列成可追溯的風險表。另列洪水樣本的季節涵蓋。","textEn":"Match construction stages to hydrologic records, distinguishing annual maxima from events in selected months. Check long-term trends and upstream regulation changes, recording stage exposure, peak uncertainty and inundation consequences in a traceable risk assessment. Document seasonal coverage of the flood sample separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以施工期洪水暴露編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以施工階段對應水文資料期間，區分全年年最大值與特定月份事件；查核長期趨勢和上游調控變更，將每階段暴露、洪峰不確定度及淹水後果列成可追溯的風險表。另列洪水樣本的季節涵蓋。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for construction-period flood exposure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Match construction stages to hydrologic records, distinguishing annual maxima from events in selected months. Check long-term trends and upstream regulation changes, recording stage exposure, peak uncertainty and inundation consequences in a traceable risk assessment. Document seasonal coverage of the flood sample separately.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「施工期洪水暴露」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Construction-period flood exposure\"?","options":["以施工階段對應水文資料期間，區分全年年最大值與特定月份事件；查核長期趨勢和上游調控變更，將每階段暴露、洪峰不確定度及淹水後果列成可追溯的風險表。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。"],"optionsEn":["Match construction stages to hydrologic records, distinguishing annual maxima from events in selected months.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以施工階段對應水文資料期間，區分全年年最大值與特定月份事件；查核長期趨勢和上游調控變更，將每階段暴露、洪峰不確定度及淹水後果列成可追溯的風險表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Match construction stages to hydrologic records, distinguishing annual maxima from events in selected months. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b240-v15-04","title":"施工期洪水暴露：失效診斷","titleEn":"Construction-period flood exposure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「施工期洪水暴露」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Construction-period flood exposure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把全年機率直接按月份等比例縮小會忽略季節集中，連續年份的氣候相關性也會破壞獨立假設。即使超越機率相同，不同階段的損失與恢復時間仍可能完全不同。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Dividing annual probability in proportion to months ignores seasonality, and climate persistence violates independence. Equal exceedance probabilities can also correspond to very different losses and recovery times at different stages of construction. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：即使超越機率相同，不同階段的損失與恢復時間仍可能完全不同。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Equal exceedance probabilities can also correspond to very different losses and recovery times at different stages of construction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把全年機率直接按月份等比例縮小會忽略季節集中，連續年份的氣候相關性也會破壞獨立假設。即使超越機率相同，不同階段的損失與恢復時間仍可能完全不同。","textEn":"Dividing annual probability in proportion to months ignores seasonality, and climate persistence violates independence. Equal exceedance probabilities can also correspond to very different losses and recovery times at different stages of construction.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「施工期洪水暴露」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Construction-period flood exposure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把全年機率直接按月份等比例縮小會忽略季節集中，連續年份的氣候相關性也會破壞獨立假設。","導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Dividing annual probability in proportion to months ignores seasonality, and climate persistence violates independence.","Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把全年機率直接按月份等比例縮小會忽略季節集中，連續年份的氣候相關性也會破壞獨立假設。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dividing annual probability in proportion to months ignores seasonality, and climate persistence violates independence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b240-v15-05","title":"明渠導流的過水能力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Open-channel diversion capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「明渠導流的過水能力」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Open-channel diversion capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"明渠能力取決於斷面、水力半徑、坡度與粗糙度，不能只看開挖面積。均勻流公式可初估穩定長渠，但入口、彎道和下游回水需要另行評估。 SI制曼寧係數n的單位為s/m^(1/3)。假設矩形渠寬10 m、水深3 m、曼寧n=0.025、坡度0.001，A=30 m²、R=30/16=1.875 m，Q=AR^(2/3)S^0.5/n=57.701 m³/s；均勻流。 局部收縮或彎道可能先控制水位，堆料和漂流物又會降低有效斷面。若只增加平均水深來滿足公式流量，可能漏掉局部溢頂或岸坡沖蝕問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「明渠導流的過水能力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Open-channel capacity depends on section, hydraulic radius, slope and roughness, not excavated area alone. Uniform-flow relations estimate a long stable reach, while entrance effects, bends and downstream backwater require separate analysis. The SI Manning coefficient n has units s/m^(1/3). Assume rectangular width 10 m, depth 3 m, Manning n=0.025 and slope 0.001. Area is 30 m² and radius 1.875 m, giving uniform-flow capacity approximately 57.701 m³/s. A contraction or bend can control stage before the uniform reach does, while stored material and debris reduce effective area. Increasing assumed average depth to meet discharge can overlook local overtopping or bank erosion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Open-channel diversion capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：SI制曼寧係數n的單位為s/m^(1/3)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The SI Manning coefficient n has units s/m^(1/3).","failure":"常見誤解：「導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「明渠導流的過水能力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Open-channel diversion capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-05-k1","title":"明渠導流的過水能力","titleEn":"Open-channel diversion capacity","text":"明渠能力取決於斷面、水力半徑、坡度與粗糙度，不能只看開挖面積。均勻流公式可初估穩定長渠，但入口、彎道和下游回水需要另行評估。","textEn":"Open-channel capacity depends on section, hydraulic radius, slope and roughness, not excavated area alone. Uniform-flow relations estimate a long stable reach, while entrance effects, bends and downstream backwater require separate analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「明渠導流的過水能力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Open-channel diversion capacity\" is correct?","options":["導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。","導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。","明渠能力取決於斷面、水力半徑、坡度與粗糙度，不能只看開挖面積。"],"optionsEn":["Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity.","Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula.","Open-channel capacity depends on section, hydraulic radius, slope and roughness, not excavated area alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"明渠能力取決於斷面、水力半徑、坡度與粗糙度，不能只看開挖面積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Open-channel capacity depends on section, hydraulic radius, slope and roughness, not excavated area alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b240-v15-06","title":"明渠導流的過水能力：定量估算","titleEn":"Open-channel diversion capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「明渠導流的過水能力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Open-channel diversion capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：SI制曼寧係數n的單位為s/m^(1/3)。假設矩形渠寬10 m、水深3 m、曼寧n=0.025、坡度0.001，A=30 m²、R=30/16=1.875 m，Q=AR^(2/3)S^0.5/n=57.701 m³/s；均勻流。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The SI Manning coefficient n has units s/m^(1/3). Assume rectangular width 10 m, depth 3 m, Manning n=0.025 and slope 0.001. Area is 30 m² and radius 1.875 m, giving uniform-flow capacity approximately 57.701 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用實測縱斷面和水面線確認是否接近均勻流，分段記錄粗糙度與阻水物；以不同尾水條件重算回水，並用流速量測核對斷面流量，不能將渠底坡直接當所有情境的能量坡。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check measured bed and water-surface profiles for near-uniform flow, recording roughness and obstructions by reach.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：SI制曼寧係數n的單位為s/m^(1/3)。假設矩形渠寬10 m、水深3 m、曼寧n=0.025、坡度0.001，A=30 m²、R=30/16=1.875 m，Q=AR^(2/3)S^0.5/n=57.701 m³/s；均勻流。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The SI Manning coefficient n has units s/m^(1/3). Assume rectangular width 10 m, depth 3 m, Manning n=0.025 and slope 0.001. Area is 30 m² and radius 1.875 m, giving uniform-flow capacity approximately 57.701 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「明渠導流的過水能力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Open-channel diversion capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：SI制曼寧係數n的單位為s/m^(1/3)。","圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。","截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The SI Manning coefficient n has units s/m^(1/3).","Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation.","During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：SI制曼寧係數n的單位為s/m^(1/3)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The SI Manning coefficient n has units s/m^(1/3). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b240-v15-07","title":"明渠導流的過水能力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Open-channel diversion capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「明渠導流的過水能力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Open-channel diversion capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用實測縱斷面和水面線確認是否接近均勻流，分段記錄粗糙度與阻水物；以不同尾水條件重算回水，並用流速量測核對斷面流量，不能將渠底坡直接當所有情境的能量坡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check measured bed and water-surface profiles for near-uniform flow, recording roughness and obstructions by reach. Recalculate backwater for different tailwaters and verify section discharge with velocities rather than assuming bed slope always equals energy slope. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以明渠導流的過水能力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用實測縱斷面和水面線確認是否接近均勻流，分段記錄粗糙度與阻水物；以不同尾水條件重算回水，並用流速量測核對斷面流量，不能將渠底坡直接當所有情境的能量坡。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for open-channel diversion capacity, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check measured bed and water-surface profiles for near-uniform flow, recording roughness and obstructions by reach. Recalculate backwater for different tailwaters and verify section discharge with velocities rather than assuming bed slope always equals energy slope.","failure":"注意干擾：局部收縮或彎道可能先控制水位，堆料和漂流物又會降低有效斷面。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A contraction or bend can control stage before the uniform reach does, while stored material and debris reduce effective area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用實測縱斷面和水面線確認是否接近均勻流，分段記錄粗糙度與阻水物；以不同尾水條件重算回水，並用流速量測核對斷面流量，不能將渠底坡直接當所有情境的能量坡。","textEn":"Check measured bed and water-surface profiles for near-uniform flow, recording roughness and obstructions by reach. Recalculate backwater for different tailwaters and verify section discharge with velocities rather than assuming bed slope always equals energy slope.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以明渠導流的過水能力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用實測縱斷面和水面線確認是否接近均勻流，分段記錄粗糙度與阻水物；以不同尾水條件重算回水，並用流速量測核對斷面流量，不能將渠底坡直接當所有情境的能量坡。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for open-channel diversion capacity, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check measured bed and water-surface profiles for near-uniform flow, recording roughness and obstructions by reach. Recalculate backwater for different tailwaters and verify section discharge with velocities rather than assuming bed slope always equals energy slope.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「明渠導流的過水能力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Open-channel diversion capacity\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用實測縱斷面和水面線確認是否接近均勻流，分段記錄粗糙度與阻水物；以不同尾水條件重算回水，並用流速量測核對斷面流量，不能將渠底坡直接當所有情境的能量坡。","基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check measured bed and water-surface profiles for near-uniform flow, recording roughness and obstructions by reach.","Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用實測縱斷面和水面線確認是否接近均勻流，分段記錄粗糙度與阻水物；以不同尾水條件重算回水，並用流速量測核對斷面流量，不能將渠底坡直接當所有情境的能量坡。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check measured bed and water-surface profiles for near-uniform flow, recording roughness and obstructions by reach. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b240-v15-08","title":"明渠導流的過水能力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Open-channel diversion capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「明渠導流的過水能力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Open-channel diversion capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部收縮或彎道可能先控制水位，堆料和漂流物又會降低有效斷面。若只增加平均水深來滿足公式流量，可能漏掉局部溢頂或岸坡沖蝕問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A contraction or bend can control stage before the uniform reach does, while stored material and debris reduce effective area. Increasing assumed average depth to meet discharge can overlook local overtopping or bank erosion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只增加平均水深來滿足公式流量，可能漏掉局部溢頂或岸坡沖蝕問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Increasing assumed average depth to meet discharge can overlook local overtopping or bank erosion.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部收縮或彎道可能先控制水位，堆料和漂流物又會降低有效斷面。若只增加平均水深來滿足公式流量，可能漏掉局部溢頂或岸坡沖蝕問題。","textEn":"A contraction or bend can control stage before the uniform reach does, while stored material and debris reduce effective area. Increasing assumed average depth to meet discharge can overlook local overtopping or bank erosion.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「明渠導流的過水能力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Open-channel diversion capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。","局部收縮或彎道可能先控制水位，堆料和漂流物又會降低有效斷面。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula.","A contraction or bend can control stage before the uniform reach does, while stored material and debris reduce effective area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部收縮或彎道可能先控制水位，堆料和漂流物又會降低有效斷面。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A contraction or bend can control stage before the uniform reach does, while stored material and debris reduce effective area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b240-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」與「入口局部損失與堵塞」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Full-flow tunnel friction loss\" and \"Entrance loss and obstruction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b240-v15-09","title":"滿流隧洞的沿程損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Full-flow tunnel friction loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Full-flow tunnel friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"導流隧洞在滿流與自由水面流之間可能轉換，水力邊界先於公式選擇。滿管沿程損失與速度平方成正比，糙率和局部缺陷會改變所需上下游能量差。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設滿流圓洞直徑6 m、長500 m、Darcy摩阻係數0.02、流量100 m³/s，v=3.537 m/s，hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=1.063 m；不含入口出口損失。 使用滿管公式卻忽略洞內自由水面和空氣囊會誤估能力，Darcy與Fanning係數混用又會差四倍。轉換流況可能出現脈動，平均能量線不能完全描述瞬間壓力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Diversion tunnels may transition between free-surface and pressurized flow, so boundary classification precedes equation choice. Full-flow friction scales with velocity squared, and roughness or defects change the required upstream-downstream energy difference. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume full circular diameter 6 m, length 500 m, Darcy factor 0.02 and discharge 100 m³/s. Velocity is 3.537 m/s and friction loss 1.063 m, excluding entrance and exit losses. Applying full-pipe relations despite free surfaces or air pockets misstates capacity, and confusing Darcy with Fanning factors introduces a factor of four. Flow transitions can pulsate, beyond what an average energy line describes. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Full-flow tunnel friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Full-flow tunnel friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-09-k1","title":"滿流隧洞的沿程損失","titleEn":"Full-flow tunnel friction loss","text":"導流隧洞在滿流與自由水面流之間可能轉換，水力邊界先於公式選擇。滿管沿程損失與速度平方成正比，糙率和局部缺陷會改變所需上下游能量差。","textEn":"Diversion tunnels may transition between free-surface and pressurized flow, so boundary classification precedes equation choice. Full-flow friction scales with velocity squared, and roughness or defects change the required upstream-downstream energy difference.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Full-flow tunnel friction loss\" is correct?","options":["導流隧洞在滿流與自由水面流之間可能轉換，水力邊界先於公式選擇。","導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。","入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。"],"optionsEn":["Diversion tunnels may transition between free-surface and pressurized flow, so boundary classification precedes equation choice.","Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula.","Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"導流隧洞在滿流與自由水面流之間可能轉換，水力邊界先於公式選擇。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Diversion tunnels may transition between free-surface and pressurized flow, so boundary classification precedes equation choice. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b240-v15-10","title":"滿流隧洞的沿程損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Full-flow tunnel friction loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Full-flow tunnel friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設滿流圓洞直徑6 m、長500 m、Darcy摩阻係數0.02、流量100 m³/s，v=3.537 m/s，hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=1.063 m；不含入口出口損失。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume full circular diameter 6 m, length 500 m, Darcy factor 0.02 and discharge 100 m³/s. Velocity is 3.537 m/s and friction loss 1.063 m, excluding entrance and exit losses. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿洞線建立壓力與能量線，確認洞頂是否持續被壓力水面覆蓋；把摩阻係數和接縫突出物分開做敏感度，並比對進出口水位與流量，檢查自由流轉滿流的遲滯。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Construct pressure and energy lines and verify whether the crown remains pressurized.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設滿流圓洞直徑6 m、長500 m、Darcy摩阻係數0.02、流量100 m³/s，v=3.537 m/s，hf=f(L/D)v²/(2g)=1.063 m；不含入口出口損失。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume full circular diameter 6 m, length 500 m, Darcy factor 0.02 and discharge 100 m³/s. Velocity is 3.537 m/s and friction loss 1.063 m, excluding entrance and exit losses.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Full-flow tunnel friction loss\", which statement holds?","options":["兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。"],"optionsEn":["Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b240-v15-11","title":"滿流隧洞的沿程損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Full-flow tunnel friction loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Full-flow tunnel friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿洞線建立壓力與能量線，確認洞頂是否持續被壓力水面覆蓋；把摩阻係數和接縫突出物分開做敏感度，並比對進出口水位與流量，檢查自由流轉滿流的遲滯。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Construct pressure and energy lines and verify whether the crown remains pressurized. Separate friction sensitivity from protruding joints, compare inlet and outlet levels with discharge, and investigate hysteresis during transitions between free-surface and full flow. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以滿流隧洞的沿程損失編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿洞線建立壓力與能量線，確認洞頂是否持續被壓力水面覆蓋；把摩阻係數和接縫突出物分開做敏感度，並比對進出口水位與流量，檢查自由流轉滿流的遲滯。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for full-flow tunnel friction loss, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Construct pressure and energy lines and verify whether the crown remains pressurized. Separate friction sensitivity from protruding joints, compare inlet and outlet levels with discharge, and investigate hysteresis during transitions between free-surface and full flow.","failure":"注意干擾：使用滿管公式卻忽略洞內自由水面和空氣囊會誤估能力，Darcy與Fanning係數混用又會差四倍。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying full-pipe relations despite free surfaces or air pockets misstates capacity, and confusing Darcy with Fanning factors introduces a factor of four. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿洞線建立壓力與能量線，確認洞頂是否持續被壓力水面覆蓋；把摩阻係數和接縫突出物分開做敏感度，並比對進出口水位與流量，檢查自由流轉滿流的遲滯。","textEn":"Construct pressure and energy lines and verify whether the crown remains pressurized. Separate friction sensitivity from protruding joints, compare inlet and outlet levels with discharge, and investigate hysteresis during transitions between free-surface and full flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以滿流隧洞的沿程損失編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿洞線建立壓力與能量線，確認洞頂是否持續被壓力水面覆蓋；把摩阻係數和接縫突出物分開做敏感度，並比對進出口水位與流量，檢查自由流轉滿流的遲滯。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for full-flow tunnel friction loss, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Construct pressure and energy lines and verify whether the crown remains pressurized. Separate friction sensitivity from protruding joints, compare inlet and outlet levels with discharge, and investigate hysteresis during transitions between free-surface and full flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Full-flow tunnel friction loss\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。","沿洞線建立壓力與能量線，確認洞頂是否持續被壓力水面覆蓋；把摩阻係數和接縫突出物分開做敏感度，並比對進出口水位與流量，檢查自由流轉滿流的遲滯。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints.","Construct pressure and energy lines and verify whether the crown remains pressurized."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沿洞線建立壓力與能量線，確認洞頂是否持續被壓力水面覆蓋；把摩阻係數和接縫突出物分開做敏感度，並比對進出口水位與流量，檢查自由流轉滿流的遲滯。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Construct pressure and energy lines and verify whether the crown remains pressurized. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b240-v15-12","title":"滿流隧洞的沿程損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Full-flow tunnel friction loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Full-flow tunnel friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用滿管公式卻忽略洞內自由水面和空氣囊會誤估能力，Darcy與Fanning係數混用又會差四倍。轉換流況可能出現脈動，平均能量線不能完全描述瞬間壓力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying full-pipe relations despite free surfaces or air pockets misstates capacity, and confusing Darcy with Fanning factors introduces a factor of four. Flow transitions can pulsate, beyond what an average energy line describes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：轉換流況可能出現脈動，平均能量線不能完全描述瞬間壓力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Flow transitions can pulsate, beyond what an average energy line describes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用滿管公式卻忽略洞內自由水面和空氣囊會誤估能力，Darcy與Fanning係數混用又會差四倍。轉換流況可能出現脈動，平均能量線不能完全描述瞬間壓力。","textEn":"Applying full-pipe relations despite free surfaces or air pockets misstates capacity, and confusing Darcy with Fanning factors introduces a factor of four. Flow transitions can pulsate, beyond what an average energy line describes.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滿流隧洞的沿程損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Full-flow tunnel friction loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["使用滿管公式卻忽略洞內自由水面和空氣囊會誤估能力，Darcy與Fanning係數混用又會差四倍。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。"],"optionsEn":["Applying full-pipe relations despite free surfaces or air pockets misstates capacity, and confusing Darcy with Fanning factors introduces a factor of four.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用滿管公式卻忽略洞內自由水面和空氣囊會誤估能力，Darcy與Fanning係數混用又會差四倍。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying full-pipe relations despite free surfaces or air pockets misstates capacity, and confusing Darcy with Fanning factors introduces a factor of four. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b240-v15-13","title":"入口局部損失與堵塞：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Entrance loss and obstruction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「入口局部損失與堵塞」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Entrance loss and obstruction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"入口把河道動能重新分配到隧洞或渠道，局部損失不只由截面大小決定。漂流物改變收縮和有效面積，速度增加又會放大損失，形成非線性的能力下降。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設原入口流速3 m/s、損失係數K=0.5，局部損失Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；同流量下有效面積減20%，速度3.75 m/s，若K不變損失增56.25%。 漂流物會同時改變K與面積，固定係數估算可能低估實際損失。偏流造成單側壓力與沖刷，即使總流量尚可，也可能已影響入口結構或鄰近岸坡。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口局部損失與堵塞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An entrance redistributes river flow into a tunnel or channel, with losses controlled by more than area. Debris changes contraction and effective opening, increasing velocity and amplifying losses nonlinearly as capacity declines. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume entrance velocity 3 m/s and loss coefficient 0.5, giving loss 0.2294 m. At constant discharge, twenty-percent area reduction raises velocity to 3.75 m/s and loss by 56.25 percent if K is unchanged. Debris changes both loss coefficient and area, so a fixed coefficient can understate deterioration. Asymmetric flow creates one-sided pressure and scour even while total discharge appears adequate, affecting the entrance and adjacent banks. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Entrance loss and obstruction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口局部損失與堵塞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Entrance loss and obstruction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-13-k1","title":"入口局部損失與堵塞","titleEn":"Entrance loss and obstruction","text":"入口把河道動能重新分配到隧洞或渠道，局部損失不只由截面大小決定。漂流物改變收縮和有效面積，速度增加又會放大損失，形成非線性的能力下降。","textEn":"An entrance redistributes river flow into a tunnel or channel, with losses controlled by more than area. Debris changes contraction and effective opening, increasing velocity and amplifying losses nonlinearly as capacity declines.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「入口局部損失與堵塞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Entrance loss and obstruction\" is correct?","options":["入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。","入口把河道動能重新分配到隧洞或渠道，局部損失不只由截面大小決定。","圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent.","An entrance redistributes river flow into a tunnel or channel, with losses controlled by more than area.","Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"入口把河道動能重新分配到隧洞或渠道，局部損失不只由截面大小決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An entrance redistributes river flow into a tunnel or channel, with losses controlled by more than area. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b240-v15-14","title":"入口局部損失與堵塞：定量估算","titleEn":"Entrance loss and obstruction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口局部損失與堵塞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Entrance loss and obstruction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設原入口流速3 m/s、損失係數K=0.5，局部損失Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；同流量下有效面積減20%，速度3.75 m/s，若K不變損失增56.25%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume entrance velocity 3 m/s and loss coefficient 0.5, giving loss 0.2294 m. At constant discharge, twenty-percent area reduction raises velocity to 3.75 m/s and loss by 56.25 percent if K is unchanged. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以入口上下游水位及局部流速重建能量差，記錄漂流物覆蓋比例和入流角度；用不同堵塞圖樣比較損失，而非只用總堵塞面積，確認是否出現偏流、旋渦與空氣捲入。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconstruct head loss from upstream and downstream levels and local velocity, recording debris coverage and approach angle.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設原入口流速3 m/s、損失係數K=0.5，局部損失Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；同流量下有效面積減20%，速度3.75 m/s，若K不變損失增56.25%。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume entrance velocity 3 m/s and loss coefficient 0.5, giving loss 0.2294 m. At constant discharge, twenty-percent area reduction raises velocity to 3.75 m/s and loss by 56.25 percent if K is unchanged.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「入口局部損失與堵塞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Entrance loss and obstruction\", which statement holds?","options":["截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。","基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged.","Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b240-v15-15","title":"入口局部損失與堵塞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Entrance loss and obstruction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口局部損失與堵塞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Entrance loss and obstruction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以入口上下游水位及局部流速重建能量差，記錄漂流物覆蓋比例和入流角度；用不同堵塞圖樣比較損失，而非只用總堵塞面積，確認是否出現偏流、旋渦與空氣捲入。檢查堵塞圖樣是否改變旋渦位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconstruct head loss from upstream and downstream levels and local velocity, recording debris coverage and approach angle. Compare different blockage patterns rather than total area alone, identifying asymmetric flow, vortices and air entrainment. Check whether blockage patterns shift vortex locations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以入口局部損失與堵塞編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以入口上下游水位及局部流速重建能量差，記錄漂流物覆蓋比例和入流角度；用不同堵塞圖樣比較損失，而非只用總堵塞面積，確認是否出現偏流、旋渦與空氣捲入。檢查堵塞圖樣是否改變旋渦位置。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for entrance loss and obstruction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Reconstruct head loss from upstream and downstream levels and local velocity, recording debris coverage and approach angle. Compare different blockage patterns rather than total area alone, identifying asymmetric flow, vortices and air entrainment. Check whether blockage patterns shift vortex locations.","failure":"注意干擾：漂流物會同時改變K與面積，固定係數估算可能低估實際損失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Debris changes both loss coefficient and area, so a fixed coefficient can understate deterioration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以入口上下游水位及局部流速重建能量差，記錄漂流物覆蓋比例和入流角度；用不同堵塞圖樣比較損失，而非只用總堵塞面積，確認是否出現偏流、旋渦與空氣捲入。檢查堵塞圖樣是否改變旋渦位置。","textEn":"Reconstruct head loss from upstream and downstream levels and local velocity, recording debris coverage and approach angle. Compare different blockage patterns rather than total area alone, identifying asymmetric flow, vortices and air entrainment. Check whether blockage patterns shift vortex locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以入口局部損失與堵塞編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以入口上下游水位及局部流速重建能量差，記錄漂流物覆蓋比例和入流角度；用不同堵塞圖樣比較損失，而非只用總堵塞面積，確認是否出現偏流、旋渦與空氣捲入。檢查堵塞圖樣是否改變旋渦位置。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for entrance loss and obstruction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Reconstruct head loss from upstream and downstream levels and local velocity, recording debris coverage and approach angle. Compare different blockage patterns rather than total area alone, identifying asymmetric flow, vortices and air entrainment. Check whether blockage patterns shift vortex locations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「入口局部損失與堵塞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Entrance loss and obstruction\"?","options":["以入口上下游水位及局部流速重建能量差，記錄漂流物覆蓋比例和入流角度；用不同堵塞圖樣比較損失，而非只用總堵塞面積，確認是否出現偏流、旋渦與空氣捲入。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。"],"optionsEn":["Reconstruct head loss from upstream and downstream levels and local velocity, recording debris coverage and approach angle.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以入口上下游水位及局部流速重建能量差，記錄漂流物覆蓋比例和入流角度；用不同堵塞圖樣比較損失，而非只用總堵塞面積，確認是否出現偏流、旋渦與空氣捲入。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconstruct head loss from upstream and downstream levels and local velocity, recording debris coverage and approach angle. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b240-v15-16","title":"入口局部損失與堵塞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Entrance loss and obstruction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口局部損失與堵塞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Entrance loss and obstruction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漂流物會同時改變K與面積，固定係數估算可能低估實際損失。偏流造成單側壓力與沖刷，即使總流量尚可，也可能已影響入口結構或鄰近岸坡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Debris changes both loss coefficient and area, so a fixed coefficient can understate deterioration. Asymmetric flow creates one-sided pressure and scour even while total discharge appears adequate, affecting the entrance and adjacent banks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：偏流造成單側壓力與沖刷，即使總流量尚可，也可能已影響入口結構或鄰近岸坡。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Asymmetric flow creates one-sided pressure and scour even while total discharge appears adequate, affecting the entrance and adjacent banks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漂流物會同時改變K與面積，固定係數估算可能低估實際損失。偏流造成單側壓力與沖刷，即使總流量尚可，也可能已影響入口結構或鄰近岸坡。","textEn":"Debris changes both loss coefficient and area, so a fixed coefficient can understate deterioration. Asymmetric flow creates one-sided pressure and scour even while total discharge appears adequate, affecting the entrance and adjacent banks.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「入口局部損失與堵塞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Entrance loss and obstruction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","漂流物會同時改變K與面積，固定係數估算可能低估實際損失。","圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Debris changes both loss coefficient and area, so a fixed coefficient can understate deterioration.","Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"漂流物會同時改變K與面積，固定係數估算可能低估實際損失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Debris changes both loss coefficient and area, so a fixed coefficient can understate deterioration. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b240-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」與「收縮流與沖刷相似」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cofferdam base uplift\" and \"Contraction flow and scour similarity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b240-v15-17","title":"圍堰底部的揚壓作用：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cofferdam base uplift: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cofferdam base uplift” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"圍堰暫時擋水不代表可忽略滲流，基底孔壓會降低有效法向力並影響抗滑。簡化三角揚壓只適用所列邊界，排水、截水和分層地基會改變實際分布。 取淡水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³。假設每米堰長底寬12 m、上游水頭8 m、下游0 m且線性衰減，揚力0.5×9.81×8×12=470.88 kN/m；堰重900 kN/m則有效重429.12 kN/m。 停抽後孔壓可能比外水位變動更快影響穩定，基底局部高壓也會被平均值掩蓋。若將堰體自重全部當摩擦法向力，會高估可動用抗滑能力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Temporary cofferdams still experience seepage, and base pressure reduces effective normal force and sliding resistance. A triangular uplift diagram applies only to stated boundaries; drains, cutoffs and layered foundations alter the actual distribution. Use freshwater unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³. Assume twelve-metre base, upstream head eight metres, zero downstream head and linear decline. Uplift is 470.88 kN/m; weight 900 kN/m leaves effective normal weight 429.12 kN/m before other forces. Pressure after pumping interruption can quickly change stability, and local high pressures disappear in averages. Treating total cofferdam weight as frictional normal force overestimates resistance because uplift reduces effective contact loading. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cofferdam base uplift” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cofferdam base uplift”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-17-k1","title":"圍堰底部的揚壓作用","titleEn":"Cofferdam base uplift","text":"圍堰暫時擋水不代表可忽略滲流，基底孔壓會降低有效法向力並影響抗滑。簡化三角揚壓只適用所列邊界，排水、截水和分層地基會改變實際分布。","textEn":"Temporary cofferdams still experience seepage, and base pressure reduces effective normal force and sliding resistance. A triangular uplift diagram applies only to stated boundaries; drains, cutoffs and layered foundations alter the actual distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cofferdam base uplift\" is correct?","options":["圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。","兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。","圍堰暫時擋水不代表可忽略滲流，基底孔壓會降低有效法向力並影響抗滑。"],"optionsEn":["Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation.","Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.","Temporary cofferdams still experience seepage, and base pressure reduces effective normal force and sliding resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"圍堰暫時擋水不代表可忽略滲流，基底孔壓會降低有效法向力並影響抗滑。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Temporary cofferdams still experience seepage, and base pressure reduces effective normal force and sliding resistance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b240-v15-18","title":"圍堰底部的揚壓作用：定量估算","titleEn":"Cofferdam base uplift: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cofferdam base uplift” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³。假設每米堰長底寬12 m、上游水頭8 m、下游0 m且線性衰減，揚力0.5×9.81×8×12=470.88 kN/m；堰重900 kN/m則有效重429.12 kN/m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³. Assume twelve-metre base, upstream head eight metres, zero downstream head and linear decline. Uplift is 470.88 kN/m; weight 900 kN/m leaves effective normal weight 429.12 kN/m before other forces. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿基底和出口配置對應剖面的水頭觀測，核對尾水與抽排水位變化；把量測分布積分後與假設三角圖比較，另查出口梯度和濁度，避免把抗滑與內部侵蝕問題混為一項。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Observe heads along the base and exit section, checking tailwater and pumping changes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³。假設每米堰長底寬12 m、上游水頭8 m、下游0 m且線性衰減，揚力0.5×9.81×8×12=470.88 kN/m；堰重900 kN/m則有效重429.12 kN/m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³. Assume twelve-metre base, upstream head eight metres, zero downstream head and linear decline. Uplift is 470.88 kN/m; weight 900 kN/m leaves effective normal weight 429.12 kN/m before other forces.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cofferdam base uplift\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³。","洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。","兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³.","Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume.","Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b240-v15-19","title":"圍堰底部的揚壓作用：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cofferdam base uplift: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cofferdam base uplift” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿基底和出口配置對應剖面的水頭觀測，核對尾水與抽排水位變化；把量測分布積分後與假設三角圖比較，另查出口梯度和濁度，避免把抗滑與內部侵蝕問題混為一項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Observe heads along the base and exit section, checking tailwater and pumping changes. Integrate measurements against the assumed triangle and assess exit gradient and turbidity separately so sliding and internal erosion are not treated as one mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以圍堰底部的揚壓作用編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿基底和出口配置對應剖面的水頭觀測，核對尾水與抽排水位變化；把量測分布積分後與假設三角圖比較，另查出口梯度和濁度，避免把抗滑與內部侵蝕問題混為一項。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for cofferdam base uplift, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Observe heads along the base and exit section, checking tailwater and pumping changes. Integrate measurements against the assumed triangle and assess exit gradient and turbidity separately so sliding and internal erosion are not treated as one mechanism.","failure":"注意干擾：停抽後孔壓可能比外水位變動更快影響穩定，基底局部高壓也會被平均值掩蓋。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Pressure after pumping interruption can quickly change stability, and local high pressures disappear in averages. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿基底和出口配置對應剖面的水頭觀測，核對尾水與抽排水位變化；把量測分布積分後與假設三角圖比較，另查出口梯度和濁度，避免把抗滑與內部侵蝕問題混為一項。","textEn":"Observe heads along the base and exit section, checking tailwater and pumping changes. Integrate measurements against the assumed triangle and assess exit gradient and turbidity separately so sliding and internal erosion are not treated as one mechanism.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以圍堰底部的揚壓作用編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。沿基底和出口配置對應剖面的水頭觀測，核對尾水與抽排水位變化；把量測分布積分後與假設三角圖比較，另查出口梯度和濁度，避免把抗滑與內部侵蝕問題混為一項。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for cofferdam base uplift, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Observe heads along the base and exit section, checking tailwater and pumping changes. Integrate measurements against the assumed triangle and assess exit gradient and turbidity separately so sliding and internal erosion are not treated as one mechanism.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cofferdam base uplift\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","沿基底和出口配置對應剖面的水頭觀測，核對尾水與抽排水位變化；把量測分布積分後與假設三角圖比較，另查出口梯度和濁度，避免把抗滑與內部侵蝕問題混為一項。","導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Observe heads along the base and exit section, checking tailwater and pumping changes.","Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"沿基底和出口配置對應剖面的水頭觀測，核對尾水與抽排水位變化；把量測分布積分後與假設三角圖比較，另查出口梯度和濁度，避免把抗滑與內部侵蝕問題混為一項。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Observe heads along the base and exit section, checking tailwater and pumping changes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b240-v15-20","title":"圍堰底部的揚壓作用：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cofferdam base uplift: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cofferdam base uplift” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"停抽後孔壓可能比外水位變動更快影響穩定，基底局部高壓也會被平均值掩蓋。若將堰體自重全部當摩擦法向力，會高估可動用抗滑能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Pressure after pumping interruption can quickly change stability, and local high pressures disappear in averages. Treating total cofferdam weight as frictional normal force overestimates resistance because uplift reduces effective contact loading. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若將堰體自重全部當摩擦法向力，會高估可動用抗滑能力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Treating total cofferdam weight as frictional normal force overestimates resistance because uplift reduces effective contact loading.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"停抽後孔壓可能比外水位變動更快影響穩定，基底局部高壓也會被平均值掩蓋。若將堰體自重全部當摩擦法向力，會高估可動用抗滑能力。","textEn":"Pressure after pumping interruption can quickly change stability, and local high pressures disappear in averages. Treating total cofferdam weight as frictional normal force overestimates resistance because uplift reduces effective contact loading.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圍堰底部的揚壓作用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cofferdam base uplift\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。","停抽後孔壓可能比外水位變動更快影響穩定，基底局部高壓也會被平均值掩蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.","Pressure after pumping interruption can quickly change stability, and local high pressures disappear in averages."],"answer":2,"explanation":"停抽後孔壓可能比外水位變動更快影響穩定，基底局部高壓也會被平均值掩蓋。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pressure after pumping interruption can quickly change stability, and local high pressures disappear in averages. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b240-v15-21","title":"收縮流與沖刷相似：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Contraction flow and scour similarity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「收縮流與沖刷相似」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contraction flow and scour similarity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"導流造成的急流與回流會重新分配河床剪力，水深弗勞德數只能描述重力慣性比例。沖刷還取決於顆粒、尾水與流況歷程，不能只憑一個無因次數直接推定深度。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設局部流速5 m/s、水深2 m，Fr=v/sqrt(gy)=1.129；教學自由水面尺度，未給粒徑與持續時間，因此不推算沖刷深度。 平均斷面流速可能漏掉貼岸高速射流，護底本身又會把沖刷轉移到末端。以某一瞬間無明顯變化判定穩定，可能忽略長時間淘刷或洪水退水期的破壞。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「收縮流與沖刷相似」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Diversion-induced jets and recirculation redistribute bed stress. Depth Froude number describes inertia relative to gravity, while scour also depends on sediment, tailwater and duration and cannot be predicted from one dimensionless number alone. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume local velocity 5 m/s and depth 2 m. Froude number is 1.129 for a free-surface scale; sediment size and duration are unspecified, so scour depth is not inferred. Section-average velocity misses bank-attached jets, while protection can shift scour to its downstream edge. Apparent short-term stability does not exclude cumulative erosion or failure during recession when support and hydraulic conditions change. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contraction flow and scour similarity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「收縮流與沖刷相似」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Contraction flow and scour similarity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-21-k1","title":"收縮流與沖刷相似","titleEn":"Contraction flow and scour similarity","text":"導流造成的急流與回流會重新分配河床剪力，水深弗勞德數只能描述重力慣性比例。沖刷還取決於顆粒、尾水與流況歷程，不能只憑一個無因次數直接推定深度。","textEn":"Diversion-induced jets and recirculation redistribute bed stress. Depth Froude number describes inertia relative to gravity, while scour also depends on sediment, tailwater and duration and cannot be predicted from one dimensionless number alone.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「收縮流與沖刷相似」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Contraction flow and scour similarity\" is correct?","options":["導流造成的急流與回流會重新分配河床剪力，水深弗勞德數只能描述重力慣性比例。","兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。","截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。"],"optionsEn":["Diversion-induced jets and recirculation redistribute bed stress.","Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.","During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"導流造成的急流與回流會重新分配河床剪力，水深弗勞德數只能描述重力慣性比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Diversion-induced jets and recirculation redistribute bed stress. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b240-v15-22","title":"收縮流與沖刷相似：定量估算","titleEn":"Contraction flow and scour similarity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「收縮流與沖刷相似」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contraction flow and scour similarity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設局部流速5 m/s、水深2 m，Fr=v/sqrt(gy)=1.129；教學自由水面尺度，未給粒徑與持續時間，因此不推算沖刷深度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume local velocity 5 m/s and depth 2 m. Froude number is 1.129 for a free-surface scale; sediment size and duration are unspecified, so scour depth is not inferred. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將床面測量與流速、尾水時序對齊，分辨局部沖刷與整體河床下降；模型試驗除弗勞德相似外還需列粒徑與黏性尺度差異，查核護底邊緣是否成為新的沖刷集中點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align bed surveys with velocity and tailwater histories, separating local scour from general degradation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設局部流速5 m/s、水深2 m，Fr=v/sqrt(gy)=1.129；教學自由水面尺度，未給粒徑與持續時間，因此不推算沖刷深度。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume local velocity 5 m/s and depth 2 m. Froude number is 1.129 for a free-surface scale; sediment size and duration are unspecified, so scour depth is not inferred.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「收縮流與沖刷相似」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Contraction flow and scour similarity\", which statement holds?","options":["基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。"],"optionsEn":["Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b240-v15-23","title":"收縮流與沖刷相似：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Contraction flow and scour similarity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「收縮流與沖刷相似」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Contraction flow and scour similarity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將床面測量與流速、尾水時序對齊，分辨局部沖刷與整體河床下降；模型試驗除弗勞德相似外還需列粒徑與黏性尺度差異，查核護底邊緣是否成為新的沖刷集中點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align bed surveys with velocity and tailwater histories, separating local scour from general degradation. In models, document sediment and viscous scale effects beyond Froude similarity and examine whether protection edges become new scour concentration points. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以收縮流與沖刷相似編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將床面測量與流速、尾水時序對齊，分辨局部沖刷與整體河床下降；模型試驗除弗勞德相似外還需列粒徑與黏性尺度差異，查核護底邊緣是否成為新的沖刷集中點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for contraction flow and scour similarity, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Align bed surveys with velocity and tailwater histories, separating local scour from general degradation. In models, document sediment and viscous scale effects beyond Froude similarity and examine whether protection edges become new scour concentration points.","failure":"注意干擾：平均斷面流速可能漏掉貼岸高速射流，護底本身又會把沖刷轉移到末端。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Section-average velocity misses bank-attached jets, while protection can shift scour to its downstream edge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將床面測量與流速、尾水時序對齊，分辨局部沖刷與整體河床下降；模型試驗除弗勞德相似外還需列粒徑與黏性尺度差異，查核護底邊緣是否成為新的沖刷集中點。","textEn":"Align bed surveys with velocity and tailwater histories, separating local scour from general degradation. In models, document sediment and viscous scale effects beyond Froude similarity and examine whether protection edges become new scour concentration points.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以收縮流與沖刷相似編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。將床面測量與流速、尾水時序對齊，分辨局部沖刷與整體河床下降；模型試驗除弗勞德相似外還需列粒徑與黏性尺度差異，查核護底邊緣是否成為新的沖刷集中點。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for contraction flow and scour similarity, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Align bed surveys with velocity and tailwater histories, separating local scour from general degradation. In models, document sediment and viscous scale effects beyond Froude similarity and examine whether protection edges become new scour concentration points.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「收縮流與沖刷相似」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Contraction flow and scour similarity\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。","將床面測量與流速、尾水時序對齊，分辨局部沖刷與整體河床下降；模型試驗除弗勞德相似外還需列粒徑與黏性尺度差異，查核護底邊緣是否成為新的沖刷集中點。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula.","Align bed surveys with velocity and tailwater histories, separating local scour from general degradation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將床面測量與流速、尾水時序對齊，分辨局部沖刷與整體河床下降；模型試驗除弗勞德相似外還需列粒徑與黏性尺度差異，查核護底邊緣是否成為新的沖刷集中點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align bed surveys with velocity and tailwater histories, separating local scour from general degradation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b240-v15-24","title":"收縮流與沖刷相似：失效診斷","titleEn":"Contraction flow and scour similarity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「收縮流與沖刷相似」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Contraction flow and scour similarity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平均斷面流速可能漏掉貼岸高速射流，護底本身又會把沖刷轉移到末端。以某一瞬間無明顯變化判定穩定，可能忽略長時間淘刷或洪水退水期的破壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Section-average velocity misses bank-attached jets, while protection can shift scour to its downstream edge. Apparent short-term stability does not exclude cumulative erosion or failure during recession when support and hydraulic conditions change. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以某一瞬間無明顯變化判定穩定，可能忽略長時間淘刷或洪水退水期的破壞。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Apparent short-term stability does not exclude cumulative erosion or failure during recession when support and hydraulic conditions change.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平均斷面流速可能漏掉貼岸高速射流，護底本身又會把沖刷轉移到末端。以某一瞬間無明顯變化判定穩定，可能忽略長時間淘刷或洪水退水期的破壞。","textEn":"Section-average velocity misses bank-attached jets, while protection can shift scour to its downstream edge. Apparent short-term stability does not exclude cumulative erosion or failure during recession when support and hydraulic conditions change.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「收縮流與沖刷相似」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Contraction flow and scour similarity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["平均斷面流速可能漏掉貼岸高速射流，護底本身又會把沖刷轉移到末端。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。"],"optionsEn":["Section-average velocity misses bank-attached jets, while protection can shift scour to its downstream edge.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均斷面流速可能漏掉貼岸高速射流，護底本身又會把沖刷轉移到末端。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Section-average velocity misses bank-attached jets, while protection can shift scour to its downstream edge. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b240-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「截流缺口的流速放大」與「洪峰暫存與水位上升」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Closure-gap velocity amplification\" and \"Flood storage and stage rise\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b240-v15-25","title":"截流缺口的流速放大：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Closure-gap velocity amplification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「截流缺口的流速放大」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Closure-gap velocity amplification” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"截流過程使剩餘缺口逐步縮小，局部流速和水面差會隨分流比例共同變動。固定流量除面積可示範敏感性，但實際河水可能轉入導流通道或上游暫存。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設瞬間缺口流量120 m³/s、水深4 m、寬由12降至8 m且分流暫不變，平均速度由2.5增至3.75 m/s；動能水頭由0.3186增至0.7167 m。 缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。只使用上一階段的水深與流量，可能低估局部射流、床面變形和材料受力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「截流缺口的流速放大」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Closure progressively narrows the remaining gap, changing velocity and head difference together with flow partition. Constant discharge divided by area illustrates sensitivity, while actual water may shift into diversion works or upstream storage. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume instantaneous gap flow 120 m³/s at depth four metres and width reducing from twelve to eight metres without repartition. Mean velocity rises from 2.5 to 3.75 m/s and velocity head from 0.3186 to 0.7167 m. Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area. Reusing previous-stage depth and flow can misrepresent local jets, bed changes and forces on closure materials. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Closure-gap velocity amplification” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「截流缺口的流速放大」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Closure-gap velocity amplification”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-25-k1","title":"截流缺口的流速放大","titleEn":"Closure-gap velocity amplification","text":"截流過程使剩餘缺口逐步縮小，局部流速和水面差會隨分流比例共同變動。固定流量除面積可示範敏感性，但實際河水可能轉入導流通道或上游暫存。","textEn":"Closure progressively narrows the remaining gap, changing velocity and head difference together with flow partition. Constant discharge divided by area illustrates sensitivity, while actual water may shift into diversion works or upstream storage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「截流缺口的流速放大」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Closure-gap velocity amplification\" is correct?","options":["截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。","截流過程使剩餘缺口逐步縮小，局部流速和水面差會隨分流比例共同變動。","洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。"],"optionsEn":["During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged.","Closure progressively narrows the remaining gap, changing velocity and head difference together with flow partition.","Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"截流過程使剩餘缺口逐步縮小，局部流速和水面差會隨分流比例共同變動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Closure progressively narrows the remaining gap, changing velocity and head difference together with flow partition. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b240-v15-26","title":"截流缺口的流速放大：定量估算","titleEn":"Closure-gap velocity amplification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「截流缺口的流速放大」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Closure-gap velocity amplification” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設瞬間缺口流量120 m³/s、水深4 m、寬由12降至8 m且分流暫不變，平均速度由2.5增至3.75 m/s；動能水頭由0.3186增至0.7167 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume instantaneous gap flow 120 m³/s at depth four metres and width reducing from twelve to eight metres without repartition. Mean velocity rises from 2.5 to 3.75 m/s and velocity head from 0.3186 to 0.7167 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步測主河道、缺口和導流口流量以閉合分流收支，配對上游水位變化核對暫存；把各施工階段幾何輸入非恆定模型，檢查固定流量近似在哪些時段失效。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure main-river, gap and diversion discharges simultaneously and compare upstream storage change to close partitioned flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設瞬間缺口流量120 m³/s、水深4 m、寬由12降至8 m且分流暫不變，平均速度由2.5增至3.75 m/s；動能水頭由0.3186增至0.7167 m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume instantaneous gap flow 120 m³/s at depth four metres and width reducing from twelve to eight metres without repartition. Mean velocity rises from 2.5 to 3.75 m/s and velocity head from 0.3186 to 0.7167 m.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「截流缺口的流速放大」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Closure-gap velocity amplification\", which statement holds?","options":["兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。","導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。"],"optionsEn":["Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints.","Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b240-v15-27","title":"截流缺口的流速放大：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Closure-gap velocity amplification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「截流缺口的流速放大」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Closure-gap velocity amplification” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步測主河道、缺口和導流口流量以閉合分流收支，配對上游水位變化核對暫存；把各施工階段幾何輸入非恆定模型，檢查固定流量近似在哪些時段失效。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure main-river, gap and diversion discharges simultaneously and compare upstream storage change to close partitioned flow. Enter stage-specific geometry into unsteady analysis and identify intervals where the constant-gap-flow approximation no longer applies. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以截流缺口的流速放大編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步測主河道、缺口和導流口流量以閉合分流收支，配對上游水位變化核對暫存；把各施工階段幾何輸入非恆定模型，檢查固定流量近似在哪些時段失效。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for closure-gap velocity amplification, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure main-river, gap and diversion discharges simultaneously and compare upstream storage change to close partitioned flow. Enter stage-specific geometry into unsteady analysis and identify intervals where the constant-gap-flow approximation no longer applies.","failure":"注意干擾：缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步測主河道、缺口和導流口流量以閉合分流收支，配對上游水位變化核對暫存；把各施工階段幾何輸入非恆定模型，檢查固定流量近似在哪些時段失效。","textEn":"Measure main-river, gap and diversion discharges simultaneously and compare upstream storage change to close partitioned flow. Enter stage-specific geometry into unsteady analysis and identify intervals where the constant-gap-flow approximation no longer applies.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以截流缺口的流速放大編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步測主河道、缺口和導流口流量以閉合分流收支，配對上游水位變化核對暫存；把各施工階段幾何輸入非恆定模型，檢查固定流量近似在哪些時段失效。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for closure-gap velocity amplification, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Measure main-river, gap and diversion discharges simultaneously and compare upstream storage change to close partitioned flow. Enter stage-specific geometry into unsteady analysis and identify intervals where the constant-gap-flow approximation no longer applies.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「截流缺口的流速放大」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Closure-gap velocity amplification\"?","options":["同步測主河道、缺口和導流口流量以閉合分流收支，配對上游水位變化核對暫存；把各施工階段幾何輸入非恆定模型，檢查固定流量近似在哪些時段失效。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。"],"optionsEn":["Measure main-river, gap and diversion discharges simultaneously and compare upstream storage change to close partitioned flow.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步測主河道、缺口和導流口流量以閉合分流收支，配對上游水位變化核對暫存；把各施工階段幾何輸入非恆定模型，檢查固定流量近似在哪些時段失效。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure main-river, gap and diversion discharges simultaneously and compare upstream storage change to close partitioned flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b240-v15-28","title":"截流缺口的流速放大：失效診斷","titleEn":"Closure-gap velocity amplification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「截流缺口的流速放大」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Closure-gap velocity amplification” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。只使用上一階段的水深與流量，可能低估局部射流、床面變形和材料受力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area. Reusing previous-stage depth and flow can misrepresent local jets, bed changes and forces on closure materials. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只使用上一階段的水深與流量，可能低估局部射流、床面變形和材料受力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reusing previous-stage depth and flow can misrepresent local jets, bed changes and forces on closure materials.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。只使用上一階段的水深與流量，可能低估局部射流、床面變形和材料受力。","textEn":"Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area. Reusing previous-stage depth and flow can misrepresent local jets, bed changes and forces on closure materials.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「截流缺口的流速放大」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Closure-gap velocity amplification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。","洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area.","Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b240-v15-29","title":"洪峰暫存與水位上升：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Flood storage and stage rise: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「洪峰暫存與水位上升」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Flood storage and stage rise” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"導流設施的瞬時出流小於洪峰時，差額會累積在上游暫存區。容量檢核需積分整個超額歷線，不能只比較洪峰差，也不能假定所有可見河谷空間都可用於儲洪。 假設超過導流能力的流量歷線為底寬2 h、峰值60 m³/s三角形，所需暫存0.5×7200×60=216000 m³；若有效面積120000 m²恆定，水位升1.8 m。 出流能力通常隨水位上升改變，固定能力三角示例可能高估或低估暫存。洪水期間地形被沖淤改變也會改寫容量，不能把一次測量曲線當作永遠有效。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洪峰暫存與水位上升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When diversion outflow falls below inflow, excess accumulates upstream. Storage checks integrate the full excess hydrograph rather than peak difference alone and cannot assume all visible valley space is available flood storage. Assume triangular excess flow lasting two hours and peaking at 60 m³/s. Required storage is 216000 m³; constant effective surface area 120000 m² gives stage rise 1.8 m, excluding changing outlet capacity. Outflow capacity usually changes with stage, making the fixed-capacity triangle potentially conservative or unconservative. Erosion and deposition can also alter storage during a flood, so one surveyed relation is not permanently valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flood storage and stage rise” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設超過導流能力的流量歷線為底寬2 h、峰值60 m³/s三角形，所需暫存0.5×7200×60=216000 m³；若有效面積120000 m²恆定，水位升1.8 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular excess flow lasting two hours and peaking at 60 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洪峰暫存與水位上升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Flood storage and stage rise”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-29-k1","title":"洪峰暫存與水位上升","titleEn":"Flood storage and stage rise","text":"導流設施的瞬時出流小於洪峰時，差額會累積在上游暫存區。容量檢核需積分整個超額歷線，不能只比較洪峰差，也不能假定所有可見河谷空間都可用於儲洪。","textEn":"When diversion outflow falls below inflow, excess accumulates upstream. Storage checks integrate the full excess hydrograph rather than peak difference alone and cannot assume all visible valley space is available flood storage.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「洪峰暫存與水位上升」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flood storage and stage rise\" is correct?","options":["洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。","基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。","導流設施的瞬時出流小於洪峰時，差額會累積在上游暫存區。"],"optionsEn":["Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume.","Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.","When diversion outflow falls below inflow, excess accumulates upstream."],"answer":2,"explanation":"導流設施的瞬時出流小於洪峰時，差額會累積在上游暫存區。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When diversion outflow falls below inflow, excess accumulates upstream. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b240-v15-30","title":"洪峰暫存與水位上升：定量估算","titleEn":"Flood storage and stage rise: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洪峰暫存與水位上升」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Flood storage and stage rise” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設超過導流能力的流量歷線為底寬2 h、峰值60 m³/s三角形，所需暫存0.5×7200×60=216000 m³；若有效面積120000 m²恆定，水位升1.8 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular excess flow lasting two hours and peaking at 60 m³/s. Required storage is 216000 m³; constant effective surface area 120000 m² gives stage rise 1.8 m, excluding changing outlet capacity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用連續方程逐時段核對入流、出流與水位容積曲線，改變時間步長檢查數值守恆；將下游回水與淹沒敏感設施疊入高程圖，確認可用暫存不是單純地形空間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check inflow, outflow and stage-storage through time and vary timestep to test numerical conservation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設超過導流能力的流量歷線為底寬2 h、峰值60 m³/s三角形，所需暫存0.5×7200×60=216000 m³；若有效面積120000 m²恆定，水位升1.8 m。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular excess flow lasting two hours and peaking at 60 m³/s. Required storage is 216000 m³; constant effective surface area 120000 m² gives stage rise 1.8 m, excluding changing outlet capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「洪峰暫存與水位上升」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flood storage and stage rise\", which statement holds?","options":["教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設超過導流能力的流量歷線為底寬2 h、峰值60 m³/s三角形，所需暫存0.5×7200×60=216000 m³。","二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。","導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular excess flow lasting two hours and peaking at 60 m³/s.","A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years.","Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設超過導流能力的流量歷線為底寬2 h、峰值60 m³/s三角形，所需暫存0.5×7200×60=216000 m³；若有效面積120000 m²恆定，水位升1.8 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular excess flow lasting two hours and peaking at 60 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b240-v15-31","title":"洪峰暫存與水位上升：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flood storage and stage rise: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洪峰暫存與水位上升」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Flood storage and stage rise” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用連續方程逐時段核對入流、出流與水位容積曲線，改變時間步長檢查數值守恆；將下游回水與淹沒敏感設施疊入高程圖，確認可用暫存不是單純地形空間。比較線性與非線性庫容曲線。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check inflow, outflow and stage-storage through time and vary timestep to test numerical conservation. Overlay downstream backwater and vulnerable facilities on elevations, verifying that usable storage is not merely an unoccupied geometric volume. Compare linear and nonlinear stage-storage representations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以洪峰暫存與水位上升編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用連續方程逐時段核對入流、出流與水位容積曲線，改變時間步長檢查數值守恆；將下游回水與淹沒敏感設施疊入高程圖，確認可用暫存不是單純地形空間。比較線性與非線性庫容曲線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for flood storage and stage rise, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check inflow, outflow and stage-storage through time and vary timestep to test numerical conservation. Overlay downstream backwater and vulnerable facilities on elevations, verifying that usable storage is not merely an unoccupied geometric volume. Compare linear and nonlinear stage-storage representations.","failure":"注意干擾：出流能力通常隨水位上升改變，固定能力三角示例可能高估或低估暫存。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Outflow capacity usually changes with stage, making the fixed-capacity triangle potentially conservative or unconservative. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用連續方程逐時段核對入流、出流與水位容積曲線，改變時間步長檢查數值守恆；將下游回水與淹沒敏感設施疊入高程圖，確認可用暫存不是單純地形空間。比較線性與非線性庫容曲線。","textEn":"Check inflow, outflow and stage-storage through time and vary timestep to test numerical conservation. Overlay downstream backwater and vulnerable facilities on elevations, verifying that usable storage is not merely an unoccupied geometric volume. Compare linear and nonlinear stage-storage representations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以洪峰暫存與水位上升編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用連續方程逐時段核對入流、出流與水位容積曲線，改變時間步長檢查數值守恆；將下游回水與淹沒敏感設施疊入高程圖，確認可用暫存不是單純地形空間。比較線性與非線性庫容曲線。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for flood storage and stage rise, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Check inflow, outflow and stage-storage through time and vary timestep to test numerical conservation. Overlay downstream backwater and vulnerable facilities on elevations, verifying that usable storage is not merely an unoccupied geometric volume. Compare linear and nonlinear stage-storage representations.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「洪峰暫存與水位上升」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flood storage and stage rise\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用連續方程逐時段核對入流、出流與水位容積曲線，改變時間步長檢查數值守恆；將下游回水與淹沒敏感設施疊入高程圖，確認可用暫存不是單純地形空間。","圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Check inflow, outflow and stage-storage through time and vary timestep to test numerical conservation.","Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用連續方程逐時段核對入流、出流與水位容積曲線，改變時間步長檢查數值守恆；將下游回水與淹沒敏感設施疊入高程圖，確認可用暫存不是單純地形空間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check inflow, outflow and stage-storage through time and vary timestep to test numerical conservation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b240-v15-32","title":"洪峰暫存與水位上升：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flood storage and stage rise: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洪峰暫存與水位上升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flood storage and stage rise” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出流能力通常隨水位上升改變，固定能力三角示例可能高估或低估暫存。洪水期間地形被沖淤改變也會改寫容量，不能把一次測量曲線當作永遠有效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Outflow capacity usually changes with stage, making the fixed-capacity triangle potentially conservative or unconservative. Erosion and deposition can also alter storage during a flood, so one surveyed relation is not permanently valid. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：洪水期間地形被沖淤改變也會改寫容量，不能把一次測量曲線當作永遠有效。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Erosion and deposition can also alter storage during a flood, so one surveyed relation is not permanently valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出流能力通常隨水位上升改變，固定能力三角示例可能高估或低估暫存。洪水期間地形被沖淤改變也會改寫容量，不能把一次測量曲線當作永遠有效。","textEn":"Outflow capacity usually changes with stage, making the fixed-capacity triangle potentially conservative or unconservative. Erosion and deposition can also alter storage during a flood, so one surveyed relation is not permanently valid.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「洪峰暫存與水位上升」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flood storage and stage rise\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。","出流能力通常隨水位上升改變，固定能力三角示例可能高估或低估暫存。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.","Outflow capacity usually changes with stage, making the fixed-capacity triangle potentially conservative or unconservative."],"answer":2,"explanation":"出流能力通常隨水位上升改變，固定能力三角示例可能高估或低估暫存。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Outflow capacity usually changes with stage, making the fixed-capacity triangle potentially conservative or unconservative. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b240-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「基坑降水與滲流供給」與「導流切換與關鍵工期」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply\" and \"Diversion transitions and critical duration\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b240-v15-33","title":"基坑降水與滲流供給：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「基坑降水與滲流供給」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"圍堰內基坑降水會增加外側水體的水頭差，抽水需求可能隨開挖深度增加。達西估算提供連續介質量級，但岩體裂隙、各向異性與河床補注需要專門辨認。 假設等效透水係數2×10⁻⁵ m/s、過流面積300 m²、水頭差10 m、路徑20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.003 m³/s即3 L/s；一維穩態且無集中裂隙。 抽水流量增加可能來自裂隙被開挖接通或施工水混入，未必是整體k變大。若只提高抽排量而不查孔壓與細料，可能掩蓋基底有效應力或侵蝕條件的改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「基坑降水與滲流供給」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dewatering inside a cofferdam increases head difference from the river, so pumping demand can grow with excavation depth. Darcy estimates provide a continuum scale, while fractures, anisotropy and riverbed recharge require distinct evidence. Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres. One-dimensional steady Darcy flow is 0.003 m³/s or three litres per second, excluding concentrated fractures. Higher pumping can reflect newly exposed fractures or process water rather than increased bulk permeability. Focusing on discharge without pressures and transported fines can conceal changes in base effective stress or internal-erosion conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設等效透水係數2×10⁻⁵ m/s、過流面積300 m²、水頭差10 m、路徑20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.003 m³/s即3 L/s；一維穩態且無集中裂隙。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres.","failure":"常見誤解：「基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「基坑降水與滲流供給」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-33-k1","title":"基坑降水與滲流供給","titleEn":"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply","text":"圍堰內基坑降水會增加外側水體的水頭差，抽水需求可能隨開挖深度增加。達西估算提供連續介質量級，但岩體裂隙、各向異性與河床補注需要專門辨認。","textEn":"Dewatering inside a cofferdam increases head difference from the river, so pumping demand can grow with excavation depth. Darcy estimates provide a continuum scale, while fractures, anisotropy and riverbed recharge require distinct evidence.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基坑降水與滲流供給」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply\" is correct?","options":["圍堰內基坑降水會增加外側水體的水頭差，抽水需求可能隨開挖深度增加。","基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。","兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。"],"optionsEn":["Dewatering inside a cofferdam increases head difference from the river, so pumping demand can grow with excavation depth.","Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.","Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"圍堰內基坑降水會增加外側水體的水頭差，抽水需求可能隨開挖深度增加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dewatering inside a cofferdam increases head difference from the river, so pumping demand can grow with excavation depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b240-v15-34","title":"基坑降水與滲流供給：定量估算","titleEn":"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「基坑降水與滲流供給」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設等效透水係數2×10⁻⁵ m/s、過流面積300 m²、水頭差10 m、路徑20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.003 m³/s即3 L/s；一維穩態且無集中裂隙。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres. One-dimensional steady Darcy flow is 0.003 m³/s or three litres per second, excluding concentrated fractures. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以抽水量、坑外孔壓和河水位同步反算等效供水，檢查停抽回復曲線辨認儲水與補注；分開雨水、施工用水及地下水收支，並記錄濁度以追查是否帶出細料。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pumping, outside piezometers and river stage to infer supply, using recovery curves to distinguish storage from recharge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設等效透水係數2×10⁻⁵ m/s、過流面積300 m²、水頭差10 m、路徑20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.003 m³/s即3 L/s；一維穩態且無集中裂隙。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres. One-dimensional steady Darcy flow is 0.003 m³/s or three litres per second, excluding concentrated fractures.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基坑降水與滲流供給」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply\", which statement holds?","options":["導流明渠只要開挖面積相同，就一定具有相同的過流能力。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設等效透水係數2×10⁻⁵ m/s、過流面積300 m²、水頭差10 m、路徑20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.003 m³/s即3 L/s。","入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。"],"optionsEn":["Diversion channels with equal excavated area necessarily have identical flow capacity.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres.","Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設等效透水係數2×10⁻⁵ m/s、過流面積300 m²、水頭差10 m、路徑20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.003 m³/s即3 L/s；一維穩態且無集中裂隙。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b240-v15-35","title":"基坑降水與滲流供給：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「基坑降水與滲流供給」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以抽水量、坑外孔壓和河水位同步反算等效供水，檢查停抽回復曲線辨認儲水與補注；分開雨水、施工用水及地下水收支，並記錄濁度以追查是否帶出細料。查核集水管是否混入地表逕流。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pumping, outside piezometers and river stage to infer supply, using recovery curves to distinguish storage from recharge. Account separately for rainfall, process water and groundwater, recording turbidity to identify possible particle transport. Check surface-runoff entry into the collection system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以基坑降水與滲流供給編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以抽水量、坑外孔壓和河水位同步反算等效供水，檢查停抽回復曲線辨認儲水與補注；分開雨水、施工用水及地下水收支，並記錄濁度以追查是否帶出細料。查核集水管是否混入地表逕流。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for excavation dewatering and seepage supply, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare pumping, outside piezometers and river stage to infer supply, using recovery curves to distinguish storage from recharge. Account separately for rainfall, process water and groundwater, recording turbidity to identify possible particle transport. Check surface-runoff entry into the collection system.","failure":"注意干擾：抽水流量增加可能來自裂隙被開挖接通或施工水混入，未必是整體k變大。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Higher pumping can reflect newly exposed fractures or process water rather than increased bulk permeability. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以抽水量、坑外孔壓和河水位同步反算等效供水，檢查停抽回復曲線辨認儲水與補注；分開雨水、施工用水及地下水收支，並記錄濁度以追查是否帶出細料。查核集水管是否混入地表逕流。","textEn":"Compare pumping, outside piezometers and river stage to infer supply, using recovery curves to distinguish storage from recharge. Account separately for rainfall, process water and groundwater, recording turbidity to identify possible particle transport. Check surface-runoff entry into the collection system.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以基坑降水與滲流供給編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。以抽水量、坑外孔壓和河水位同步反算等效供水，檢查停抽回復曲線辨認儲水與補注；分開雨水、施工用水及地下水收支，並記錄濁度以追查是否帶出細料。查核集水管是否混入地表逕流。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for excavation dewatering and seepage supply, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare pumping, outside piezometers and river stage to infer supply, using recovery curves to distinguish storage from recharge. Account separately for rainfall, process water and groundwater, recording turbidity to identify possible particle transport. Check surface-runoff entry into the collection system.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基坑降水與滲流供給」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。","以抽水量、坑外孔壓和河水位同步反算等效供水，檢查停抽回復曲線辨認儲水與補注；分開雨水、施工用水及地下水收支，並記錄濁度以追查是否帶出細料。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.","Compare pumping, outside piezometers and river stage to infer supply, using recovery curves to distinguish storage from recharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以抽水量、坑外孔壓和河水位同步反算等效供水，檢查停抽回復曲線辨認儲水與補注；分開雨水、施工用水及地下水收支，並記錄濁度以追查是否帶出細料。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pumping, outside piezometers and river stage to infer supply, using recovery curves to distinguish storage from recharge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b240-v15-36","title":"基坑降水與滲流供給：失效診斷","titleEn":"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「基坑降水與滲流供給」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"抽水流量增加可能來自裂隙被開挖接通或施工水混入，未必是整體k變大。若只提高抽排量而不查孔壓與細料，可能掩蓋基底有效應力或侵蝕條件的改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Higher pumping can reflect newly exposed fractures or process water rather than increased bulk permeability. Focusing on discharge without pressures and transported fines can conceal changes in base effective stress or internal-erosion conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若只提高抽排量而不查孔壓與細料，可能掩蓋基底有效應力或侵蝕條件的改變。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Focusing on discharge without pressures and transported fines can conceal changes in base effective stress or internal-erosion conditions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"抽水流量增加可能來自裂隙被開挖接通或施工水混入，未必是整體k變大。若只提高抽排量而不查孔壓與細料，可能掩蓋基底有效應力或侵蝕條件的改變。","textEn":"Higher pumping can reflect newly exposed fractures or process water rather than increased bulk permeability. Focusing on discharge without pressures and transported fines can conceal changes in base effective stress or internal-erosion conditions.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基坑降水與滲流供給」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Excavation dewatering and seepage supply\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["抽水流量增加可能來自裂隙被開挖接通或施工水混入，未必是整體k變大。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。"],"optionsEn":["Higher pumping can reflect newly exposed fractures or process water rather than increased bulk permeability.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽水流量增加可能來自裂隙被開挖接通或施工水混入，未必是整體k變大。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Higher pumping can reflect newly exposed fractures or process water rather than increased bulk permeability. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b240-v15-37","title":"導流切換與關鍵工期：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Diversion transitions and critical duration: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「導流切換與關鍵工期」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diversion transitions and critical duration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"導流切換把水工能力和施工排程連在一起，某項延誤會讓高暴露階段跨入不同水文季節。關鍵路徑需表示真正的前置關係，並與可回復狀態和監測交接共同審查。 假設入口工程18 days、隧洞檢查12 days可平行，兩者完成後切換5 days，再驗證3 days，總期max(18,12)+5+3=26 days；入口延誤4 days使總期30 days。 名義平行的工作可能共享設備或通道，隱藏資源限制會使計算工期過短。若把驗證當成可壓縮空檔，可能在尚未證明新通道能力時就失去原來的導流冗餘。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導流切換與關鍵工期」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Diversion transitions couple hydraulic capacity with scheduling, and delays can carry vulnerable stages into a different hydrologic season. Critical paths must represent actual dependencies and be reviewed with recoverable states and monitoring handover requirements. Assume entrance work eighteen days and tunnel checks twelve days run in parallel, followed by transition five days and verification three days. Duration is 26 days; four-day entrance delay increases it to thirty days. Nominally parallel tasks may share equipment or access, so hidden resource constraints shorten calculated duration unrealistically. Treating verification as expendable slack can remove previous diversion redundancy before the new route has demonstrated capacity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diversion transitions and critical duration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設入口工程18 days、隧洞檢查12 days可平行，兩者完成後切換5 days，再驗證3 days，總期max(18,12)+5+3=26 days；入口延誤4 days使總期30 days。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume entrance work eighteen days and tunnel checks twelve days run in parallel, followed by transition five days and verification three days.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導流切換與關鍵工期」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diversion transitions and critical duration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-37-k1","title":"導流切換與關鍵工期","titleEn":"Diversion transitions and critical duration","text":"導流切換把水工能力和施工排程連在一起，某項延誤會讓高暴露階段跨入不同水文季節。關鍵路徑需表示真正的前置關係，並與可回復狀態和監測交接共同審查。","textEn":"Diversion transitions couple hydraulic capacity with scheduling, and delays can carry vulnerable stages into a different hydrologic season. Critical paths must represent actual dependencies and be reviewed with recoverable states and monitoring handover requirements.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導流切換與關鍵工期」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Diversion transitions and critical duration\" is correct?","options":["兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。","導流切換把水工能力和施工排程連在一起，某項延誤會讓高暴露階段跨入不同水文季節。","二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。"],"optionsEn":["Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints.","Diversion transitions couple hydraulic capacity with scheduling, and delays can carry vulnerable stages into a different hydrologic season.","A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years."],"answer":1,"explanation":"導流切換把水工能力和施工排程連在一起，某項延誤會讓高暴露階段跨入不同水文季節。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Diversion transitions couple hydraulic capacity with scheduling, and delays can carry vulnerable stages into a different hydrologic season. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b240-v15-38","title":"導流切換與關鍵工期：定量估算","titleEn":"Diversion transitions and critical duration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導流切換與關鍵工期」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diversion transitions and critical duration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設入口工程18 days、隧洞檢查12 days可平行，兩者完成後切換5 days，再驗證3 days，總期max(18,12)+5+3=26 days；入口延誤4 days使總期30 days。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume entrance work eighteen days and tunnel checks twelve days run in parallel, followed by transition five days and verification three days. Duration is 26 days; four-day entrance delay increases it to thirty days. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用每項實際完成條件建立前置網路，核對檢查簽認是否真能與施工平行；將總期疊上季節洪水暴露，演練延誤如何改變可用導流狀態，保留更新責任與水文觸發的審查紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build dependencies from actual completion criteria and verify whether inspections can truly run in parallel with work.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設入口工程18 days、隧洞檢查12 days可平行，兩者完成後切換5 days，再驗證3 days，總期max(18,12)+5+3=26 days；入口延誤4 days使總期30 days。","textEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume entrance work eighteen days and tunnel checks twelve days run in parallel, followed by transition five days and verification three days. Duration is 26 days; four-day entrance delay increases it to thirty days.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導流切換與關鍵工期」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Diversion transitions and critical duration\", which statement holds?","options":["導流隧洞的摩阻係數不分Darcy或Fanning定義都能直接代入同一公式。","圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。","教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設入口工程18 days、隧洞檢查12 days可平行，兩者完成後切換5 days，再驗證3 days，總期max(18,12)+5+3=26 days。"],"optionsEn":["Darcy and Fanning friction factors can be used interchangeably in the same tunnel formula.","Because a cofferdam is temporary, uplift can be omitted from its sliding calculation.","Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume entrance work eighteen days and tunnel checks twelve days run in parallel, followed by transition five days and verification three days."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設入口工程18 days、隧洞檢查12 days可平行，兩者完成後切換5 days，再驗證3 days，總期max(18,12)+5+3=26 days；入口延誤4 days使總期30 days。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume entrance work eighteen days and tunnel checks twelve days run in parallel, followed by transition five days and verification three days. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b240-v15-39","title":"導流切換與關鍵工期：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion transitions and critical duration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導流切換與關鍵工期」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diversion transitions and critical duration” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用每項實際完成條件建立前置網路，核對檢查簽認是否真能與施工平行；將總期疊上季節洪水暴露，演練延誤如何改變可用導流狀態，保留更新責任與水文觸發的審查紀錄。把共用設備占用列入排程。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build dependencies from actual completion criteria and verify whether inspections can truly run in parallel with work. Overlay duration on seasonal exposure and examine how delays change available diversion states, recording update responsibility and hydrologically triggered review decisions. Include shared-equipment occupancy explicitly in the schedule. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以導流切換與關鍵工期編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用每項實際完成條件建立前置網路，核對檢查簽認是否真能與施工平行；將總期疊上季節洪水暴露，演練延誤如何改變可用導流狀態，保留更新責任與水文觸發的審查紀錄。把共用設備占用列入排程。","observationEn":"Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for diversion transitions and critical duration, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Build dependencies from actual completion criteria and verify whether inspections can truly run in parallel with work. Overlay duration on seasonal exposure and examine how delays change available diversion states, recording update responsibility and hydrologically triggered review decisions. Include shared-equipment occupancy explicitly in the schedule.","failure":"注意干擾：名義平行的工作可能共享設備或通道，隱藏資源限制會使計算工期過短。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Nominally parallel tasks may share equipment or access, so hidden resource constraints shorten calculated duration unrealistically. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用每項實際完成條件建立前置網路，核對檢查簽認是否真能與施工平行；將總期疊上季節洪水暴露，演練延誤如何改變可用導流狀態，保留更新責任與水文觸發的審查紀錄。把共用設備占用列入排程。","textEn":"Build dependencies from actual completion criteria and verify whether inspections can truly run in parallel with work. Overlay duration on seasonal exposure and examine how delays change available diversion states, recording update responsibility and hydrologically triggered review decisions. Include shared-equipment occupancy explicitly in the schedule.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以導流切換與關鍵工期編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。用每項實際完成條件建立前置網路，核對檢查簽認是否真能與施工平行；將總期疊上季節洪水暴露，演練延誤如何改變可用導流狀態，保留更新責任與水文觸發的審查紀錄。把共用設備占用列入排程。","textEn":"Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for diversion transitions and critical duration, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Build dependencies from actual completion criteria and verify whether inspections can truly run in parallel with work. Overlay duration on seasonal exposure and examine how delays change available diversion states, recording update responsibility and hydrologically triggered review decisions. Include shared-equipment occupancy explicitly in the schedule.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導流切換與關鍵工期」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Diversion transitions and critical duration\"?","options":["用每項實際完成條件建立前置網路，核對檢查簽認是否真能與施工平行；將總期疊上季節洪水暴露，演練延誤如何改變可用導流狀態，保留更新責任與水文觸發的審查紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。"],"optionsEn":["Build dependencies from actual completion criteria and verify whether inspections can truly run in parallel with work.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用每項實際完成條件建立前置網路，核對檢查簽認是否真能與施工平行；將總期疊上季節洪水暴露，演練延誤如何改變可用導流狀態，保留更新責任與水文觸發的審查紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build dependencies from actual completion criteria and verify whether inspections can truly run in parallel with work. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b240-v15-40","title":"導流切換與關鍵工期：失效診斷","titleEn":"Diversion transitions and critical duration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"prerequisiteIds":["b240-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導流切換與關鍵工期」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diversion transitions and critical duration” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"名義平行的工作可能共享設備或通道，隱藏資源限制會使計算工期過短。若把驗證當成可壓縮空檔，可能在尚未證明新通道能力時就失去原來的導流冗餘。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Nominally parallel tasks may share equipment or access, so hidden resource constraints shorten calculated duration unrealistically. Treating verification as expendable slack can remove previous diversion redundancy before the new route has demonstrated capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：若把驗證當成可壓縮空檔，可能在尚未證明新通道能力時就失去原來的導流冗餘。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Treating verification as expendable slack can remove previous diversion redundancy before the new route has demonstrated capacity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b240-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"名義平行的工作可能共享設備或通道，隱藏資源限制會使計算工期過短。若把驗證當成可壓縮空檔，可能在尚未證明新通道能力時就失去原來的導流冗餘。","textEn":"Nominally parallel tasks may share equipment or access, so hidden resource constraints shorten calculated duration unrealistically. Treating verification as expendable slack can remove previous diversion redundancy before the new route has demonstrated capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]},{"id":"b240-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導流切換與關鍵工期」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Diversion transitions and critical duration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","名義平行的工作可能共享設備或通道，隱藏資源限制會使計算工期過短。","二十年重現期洪水表示施工開始後前十九年都不可能發生。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Nominally parallel tasks may share equipment or access, so hidden resource constraints shorten calculated duration unrealistically.","A twenty-year return period means that flood cannot occur during the first nineteen years."],"answer":1,"explanation":"名義平行的工作可能共享設備或通道，隱藏資源限制會使計算工期過短。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Nominally parallel tasks may share equipment or access, so hidden resource constraints shorten calculated duration unrealistically. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usace-coffer","v15s-usbr-construction","b-src-water","v15s-usbr-manuals"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
